Changes made
------------

scripts/import-devices.mjs converts the dataset's CSV files into the JSON this
application reads. The data is not edited, but the format is:

  - Each device's rows become one JSON file, described by devices/schema.json.
  - The nrpn_msb and nrpn_lsb columns are folded into a single 14-bit number.
  - Rows carrying a cc_lsb become a "cc14" parameter holding both CC numbers.
    The documented range is carried through as-is and not reinterpreted.
  - A row documenting both a CC and an NRPN is imported as the CC.
  - Rows documenting neither a CC nor an NRPN are omitted, as are rows whose
    values fall outside what devices/schema.json can express.
  - Note trigger files (*.triggers.csv) are not imported.
  - An "enabled" field is added, set on every parameter, which the application
    uses to decide what to randomise.

As Pencil Research note, portions of the dataset that refer to specific
devices may be owned by those devices' respective manufacturers.
